-- title:
--   Origin-chart sections are compatible under Proj base change
-- statement:
--   Let $T$ and $T'$ be commutative rings, let $W$ be a projective Weierstrass curve over $T$, let $f : T \to T'$ be a ring homomorphism, and let $\varphi$ be a homomorphism of graded rings from `projModelGradingCR W` to `projModelGradingCR (W.map f)`, i.e. between the induced $\mathbb{N}$-gradings on the quotients of $\mathrm{MvPolynomial}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\,3)$ by the ideal generated by the Weierstrass cubic of $W$, respectively of $W.map f$. Assume the irrelevant ideal of the target grading is contained in the image under $\varphi$ of the irrelevant ideal of the source grading, so that `Proj.map φ hφ : Proj (projModelGradingCR (W.map f)) ⟶ Proj (projModelGradingCR W)` is defined, and assume `IsCoefficientHom W f φ`: $\varphi$ carries the class of a constant $C\,a$ to the class of $C\,(f a)$ for every $a \in T$, and the class of each coordinate $X_i$, $i \in \mathrm{Fin}\,3$, to the class of $X_i$. Let $P$ be a section of the projective model of $W$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,T$ and $P'$ a section of the projective model of $W.map f$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,T'$. Suppose $\chi$ is a ring homomorphism from the degree-zero homogeneous localisation `OriginChartRing W` at the coordinate of index $1$ to $T$ such that $P$ factors as $\mathrm{Spec}(\chi)$ followed by the open immersion of the origin chart, and such that $\chi$ kills both `xOverY W` and `zOverY W`; suppose $\chi'$ satisfies the corresponding three conditions for $P'$ over $T'$. Then $P'$ followed by `Proj.map φ hφ` equals $\mathrm{Spec}(f)$ followed by $P$, as morphisms $\mathrm{Spec}\,T' \to \mathrm{Proj}\,$`(projModelGradingCR W)`.
--
--   This is the base-change compatibility of the origin section $(0 : 1 : 0)$ of a Weierstrass projective model: sections cut out in the chart where the second coordinate is inverted and at which both $x/y$ and $z/y$ vanish are matched by the morphism of $\mathrm{Proj}$'s induced by a coefficient-wise graded homomorphism. It is used in the construction of the group law on the global Drinfeld model, in particular in the commutativity argument at the identity, and in the level-structure constructions for modular curves where a Tate point must be identified with the origin after base change.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_DrinfeldGlobal_comp_projMap_eq_of_isOriginChartSection.lean

